It can't just be an individual responsibility. I'm wondering, Sihan, if we can talk a moment about some of the work that's looked at airline cockpits, for example, compared to 50 or 60 years ago, airline cockpits today are designed to assume that pilots are going to make mistakes. The goal of the cockpit is not to say, unless you're perfect, something bad is going to happen to you. The goal of the cockpit now is to say, we know that things are going to fail from time to time. We know that pilots are going to make mistakes. The goal of the cockpit now is to minimize those mistakes.
谈论他们犯过的错误，以任何某种程度上让人们可以犯错误并学习和成长的方式。你想讨论的是，如何才能做到这一点——我们教育人们如何将事故发生时的影响降到最低，或者如何将伤害降到最低，以及如何从中吸取教训，如何大声说出来，并知道一个错误并不是世界末日。

100
00:47:53.000 --> 00:48:26.000
